YAAP -- Fleshpile IV -- Cha Elf Pri

Ascension number 4, and my THIRD since Christmas Eve (5 weeks).
I am on a winning streak! I've dabbled with priests here and
there, always liked them but never had much luck. This time, I
went all the way :).

It started with a very large bookstore on DL2, dipped the
identify scrolls and got a full ID on most scrolls and a handful
of spellbooks. I love when that happens early :). I skipped the
Gnome mines and went down to Delphi on 9, and then Sokoban on
10. Found an amulet in Sokoban, then headed back to 4 to do the
mines. Went down to the mall, didn't find anything interesting.
There was a lich on the level right beneath the mall that
destroyed my robe, so I turned around. Never did finish the
mines this game, but I had found a luckstone already anyway so
no biggie.

Found an altar on 14, set up a headquarters there and started
clearing out the levels nearby and reporting back frequently to
hoard. Had quite a few divination spells by this time, including
Detect Treasure & Monsters, so I had an easy time exploring and
being careful.

Ludios was on 19, cleared that out and got the usual riches.
Found an aligned temple on 21, so I moved my HQ to there and got
my unarmored AC to -1.

By now I have 2 amulets of life saving, around +2 or so on all
my armor, +2 and +5 rings of increase damage, and 3 magic
markers. Genocided Mind Flayers & Liches, and got my mace up to
+6. All my markers are dry :(.

Headed down to Medusa, ended up getting triple-teamed by eels.
One wrapped around me, and I didn't know which of the 3 it was.
Ended up dying twice to those eels, using both my amulets.
In the castle, I used the wand to replace my robe, got gauntlets
of dex (and discovered that I already had a +0 one in my pack,
oops), a blessed book of identification (wish I had done that
first! Oops again), Gray dragon scale, Charging scrolls, and I
don't remember what else.

Headed back to HQ to suit up for the quest, then headed back to
16 to enter it. The quest was a breeze, with my 2 rings of increase
damage I was dropping everything pretty quickly. There were SO many
wraiths in there! I gained 5 levels by the time I got to the nemesis.

Had to chase the boss up a few stairs, but eventually got on the
up-stair and took him out. Got the Mitre and headed back to HQ
Used a charging scroll to get my marker back up, and enchanted
my mitre a bit. Used a cursed genocide scroll to teleport in
some naughty nurses and had a little orgy. Whee! Also did a
bunch of alchemy for about 18 blessed full healing potions, got
my HP up to arould 350 or so (maybe more, I think that was about
it). Realized I only had 6 candles, so ran back to the mines
real fast and picked up 8 more (it's good to have a backup
set!).

Headed down to Gehennom, since I had Magic Mapping, Detect
Treasure & Detect Monster, I had no problem at all with it.
Jeez, it's SO much easier with a caster than a fighter!

A disenchanter reduced my mace down to +1, so I ended up doing
quite a chunk of Gehennom with a rotten +1 mace. I felt so
inadequate. Eventually found another magic marker, so I headed
back and got it to +7, as well as maxing out all my armor
(finally) and charging my +2 increase damage ring to +4.

I found a bones pile down in Gehennom from an old Samurai (I had
posted about the importance of magic resistance when he had died
-- See my other post), and got Magicbane off it plus a bunch of
relatively unimportant stuff.

Vlad's was on Orcus' level, so I marked it to come back later.
This is where I panicked for a bit. I ended up falling through a
hole, and had to come up from below to meet Orcus. Since I'm too
chicken to wield cockatrices, I went for a brain-smashing on him
instead of the easy way. So, I fought my way to the up stair to
challenge him. On the way, he summoned Yeenoghu, and they were
tag-teaming me. I got to the up-stair successfully, started
bashing them...

And Yeenoghu summons Demogorgon. Yikes! I had never seen him
before, so I panicked and consulted the spoiler. Lucky I had
found that Magicbane! I did an Elbereth, horned myself, and
proceeded to tank Demogorgon, Orcus, and Yeenoghu
simultaneously. I'd like to christen that "The Great Battle of
Orcus Town" if I may ;).

Anyway, finished that up, mapped down to G18, and cast Light on
the Vibrating Square. Went back up and took out Vlad (easily, as
always), and then the wizard. He went down to a Death wand, and
I went down to the Vibrating Square. 1, 2, 3, poof, and I
descend.

The ring of Conflict makes areas like this so much easier! Rang
the bell a few times and found the temple entrance, and went in
to face the Priest. I was level 24 by now with just under 500hp,
but that priest is pretty badass. He got me down to 64hp! I was
scared, lemme tell ya. Luckily I had saved one potion of full
healing for just this eventuality! Tossed that back, and I'm
back to full. Just to add insult to the priest, I backed off and
let a nearby Sargeant kill him with his silver saber. Ha! Thank
you Conflict! Got the amulet, named it, and headed out.

Only got hit by the force twice! That's a record ;). Got out and
back to HQ, loaded up my gems, wands and artifacts, and headed
up to the surface.

Drank some booze and detected gold on Earth, Water and Air, but
just floated around on Fire since it's usually pretty easy to
find the portal there. Jeez I hate fire though, so slow from all
the animations.

Onto astral, I introduced the anti-conflict angels to my +7
mace. Blinded, I see Death is in the middle, so I go right.
Zapping death and teleport in all directions, I cut my way to
the right-hand altar, and find it's Lawful. So, I head back,
killing Pestilence on the way. I wanna go middle, but I see
Death is still there, so I go left instead. Zap zap zap, into
the Left temple, that's it! #offer, happiness.
